// ============================================================================
//  mod_spas.zone  -  the campaign SPAS-12, v2.9.18 (user request 2026-08-31)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Every asset here resolves from nicaragua.ff, which build_ff.bat has always
//  --load'ed LAST - so by first-load-wins nothing shared can change owner; the
//  only names taken from it are ones no zombies fastfile carries at all. The
//  defs are raw runtime files in weapons\zm (spas_zm 17,533 B / spas_upgraded_zm
//  17,543 B, both under the 20,480 ceiling after the tar21qol/fiveseven trims);
//  camo_spas ships as a raw 13-slot JSON (the SP asset is 4-slot - the exact
//  Green Run animated-camo failure - extended with camo_870mcs's slots 5-13
//  over the spas's own three camo-able materials).
//
//  Sounds need NOTHING shipped: the campaign gun's own fire audio is the
//  srm1216 payload (measured - wpn_spas_fire_plr's FileSource in the SP bank
//  is wpn\shotgun\srm1216\plr\shot\wpn_srm1216_fire), and the srm1216
//  aliases are resident on all six zombies maps, so the defs name those and
//  the audio is byte-identical to the campaign gun everywhere - the user's
//  sound pack keeps authority. The fly_spas_* reload foley in the notetracks
//  is resident on five maps; on Origins the reload is quiet, the same class
//  of gap the README already documents for stock's own claymore plant.
//
//  menu_mp_weapons_spas (the def's hudIcon) is deliberately NOT shipped -
//  mod_locations.zone's own note: create-a-class icons that zombies never
//  draws.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,t6_wpn_shotty_spas_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_shotty_spas_world
material,mc/mtl_t6_wpn_shotty_spas_camo1
